WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.580
In 1785, Immanuel Kant pictured
a dealer who never overcharges,

2
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.500
so that even a child gets a fair price.

3
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.070
Customers are honestly served.

4
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.150
But why is he honest?

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.460
In 2015, Volkswagen, which
advertised clean diesel,

6
00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.400
was exposed for cheating emissions tests.

7
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.770
So if a company does good
only because it pays,

8
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.230
has it done anything good at all?

9
00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.120
In this mission, you'll test business decisions
with Kant's ideas and with utilitarian

10
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.130
thinking.

11
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:37.570
Then you'll weigh whether people can truly
flourish in a world of profit and shopping.

12
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:42.630
Your mission: weigh up whether good done
only because it pays still counts as

13
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:43.230
good.
